From: NanoKVM OS maintainers <maintainers@nanokvm.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Exclude timed VI diagnostic sampling from load average

The one-second sampling delay is not resource contention. Preserve the full
sampling interval and monotonic FPS calculation, but sleep in TASK_IDLE.

--- a/interdrv/vi/chip/cv180x/proc/vi_dbg_proc.c
+++ b/interdrv/vi/chip/cv180x/proc/vi_dbg_proc.c
@@ -44,7 +44,14 @@
 	 * This does not reprogram CSI or change the capture ownership model.
 	 */
 	t1 = ktime_get_ns();
-	msleep(1000);
+	/* Diagnostic delay, not an uninterruptible resource wait. Keep the
+	 * complete interval even if another wakeup arrives early.
+	 */
+	{
+		long remaining = msecs_to_jiffies(1000);
+		while (remaining > 0)
+			remaining = schedule_timeout_idle(remaining);
+	}
 	for (raw_num = ISP_PRERAW_A; raw_num < ISP_PRERAW_VIRT_MAX; raw_num++) {
 		if (!ctx->isp_pipe_enable[raw_num])
 			continue;
